# race-4p-vs: VS BATTLE 4 PLAYERS on Mute City, split screen, under [debug] pads=4.
# Requires `--ini pads=4`: the 3DS has one pad and the decomp gates VS on the port count
# (decomp/src/overlays/ovl_i6/main_menu.c:205 and :317-324). Ports 2-4 mirror port 1
# (port/input_bridge.c), so the four machines drive together -- deterministic, and it is
# the split-screen viewports that this replay exists to draw.
# Modes: 7 MAIN_MENU -> 10 COURSE_SELECT -> 8 MACHINE_SELECT -> 9 MACHINE_SETTINGS -> 5 VS_4P.
# SHOT PLACEMENT IS NOT AUTHORED HERE ANY MORE (NEXT.md B15/B43, coverage2-progress.md).
# This file is the INPUT script: ticks, buttons, sticks. The schedule that decides which frames
# the parity gate hashes is DERIVED from a `[debug] cov=1` coverage census of the replay and
# written into the .gdxrec by tools/dev/covsched.py. Regenerating a .gdxrec from this file
# therefore produces a recording with NO SHOTs; re-apply the schedule with
#   tools/dev/covsched.py derive <cov-run>/log-*.txt --rewrite in.gdxrec out.gdxrec
# The hand-placed schedules this file used to carry covered 49-80% of what their replay draws.
build native/replays@dd936b2
seed1 0x1234abcd
seed2 0x0fedcba9
pins renderthread=0 rival_detail_auto=0 stereo=1 fh_every=0 pads=4
at 400
press START 15 0
at 660
press RIGHT 12 0
at 760
press RIGHT 12 0
at 860
press RIGHT 12 0
at 960
wait 1
at 1060
press A 12 0
at 1180
wait 1
